### 2. Plan Type Patterns — Batch Cache Plans Disproportionately Affected

Batch-cache plans (HMO Classic, PPO Select, CHIP) are implicated in **6 of the 10 defects**:

- **CARE-PBC-002** — HMO Classic and CHIP showing "Live data" label *(direct batch-cache failure)*
- **CARE-PBC-003** — PPO Select and Standard Plan *(deductible-phase display)*
- **CARE-PBC-007** — PPO Select and HMO Classic missing ACA disclaimer *(38% of member population)*
- **CARE-PBC-009** — PPO Select + Standard Plan combination *(plan-switch)*
- **CARE-PBC-010** — CHIP plan Unix epoch timestamp *(batch cache null state)*
- **CARE-PBC-005** — All plan types under concurrent load

**Implication:** The batch-cache data path was a known complexity flagged in the M3 requirements — the nightly cache, the timestamp requirement, and the plan-type detection logic all interact. The defect data confirms that this path received insufficient test coverage across its full state space. Specifically: the state where batch cache has NOT yet run (null state), the state where the wrong label is applied, and the state where plan-type switching invalidates cached data — all escaped the test suite.

