### 5. Top 3 Test Coverage Gaps Implied by This Defect Batch

**Gap 1 — Batch cache null/empty state testing (implies CARE-PBC-010, CARE-PBC-002)**
No test case validated what the system displays when the batch cache has not yet run or returns a null timestamp. EC-04 in our edge case suite flagged this risk — it was not executed or was not in the original test suite at all.

**Gap 2 — Compliance display testing across ALL plan types (implies CARE-PBC-007, CARE-PBC-002)**
The ACA disclaimer test was designed but apparently only validated on Carelon Standard Plan. Batch-cache plan members (PPO Select, HMO Classic) were not covered in the compliance display test pass. A test matrix covering all plan type × compliance field combinations was absent.

**Gap 3 — Error state and fallback UI testing (implies CARE-PBC-004, CARE-PBC-005, CARE-PBC-010)**
Three separate defects produced blank pages or incorrect system state with no graceful fallback. Session expiry, API timeout, and null timestamp all needed dedicated negative test cases that either didn't exist or weren't executed. The absence of a "what does the system show when X fails?" test for each critical system dependency is the single largest gap in the test suite.

